{"name":"Money","hex":"#7b9a6d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Money","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","An unincorporated community in Leflore County, Mississippi, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Money"}],"entries":[{"title":"Money","blocks":[{"text":"Money is any item or verifiable record that is generally accepted as payment for goods and services and repayment of debts, such as taxes, in a particular country or socio-economic context. The primary functions which distinguish money are: medium of exchange, a unit of account, a store of value and sometimes, a standard of deferred payment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Euro_coins_and_banknotes_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Euro_coins_and_banknotes_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Money","wikidata":"Q1368"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/BMC_06.jpg/330px-BMC_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/BMC_06.jpg/330px-BMC_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 640 BC one-third stater electrum coin from Lydia.  According to Herodotus, the Lydians were the first people to introduce the use of gold and silver coins.[5] It is thought by modern scholars that these first stamped coins were minted around 650 to 600 BC.[6]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABMC_06.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Gold_Stater_of_Pharaoh_Nektanebo_II.jpg/500px-Gold_Stater_of_Pharaoh_Nektanebo_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Gold_Stater_of_Pharaoh_Nektanebo_II.jpg/500px-Gold_Stat